WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.752 --> 00:00:11.832
<v><b>Female Speaker 1:</b></v> Modern crime novels are very different from the stories of the past.

2
00:00:12.018 --> 00:00:21.170
These days, the main characters aren’t only private investigators – they’re also FBI agents or journalists.

3
00:00:21.511 --> 00:00:26.374
In some stories, there’s a group of people trying to catch a criminal,

4
00:00:26.482 --> 00:00:32.522
and in other stories, the detectives are either older or younger than usual.

5
00:00:36.673 --> 00:00:40.359
<v><b>Male Speaker 1:</b></v> Going to live in a new place can be very exciting,

6
00:00:40.467 --> 00:00:42.697
but it’s also a lot of work.

7
00:00:42.914 --> 00:00:46.786
The first thing to do is pack all your things into boxes.

8
00:00:46.863 --> 00:00:50.890
Write on each box which room it’s for and what’s inside.

9
00:00:51.091 --> 00:00:57.441
Put the furniture in your new place before you take the boxes – that makes it easier to find your things.

10
00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:06.314
<v><b>Female Speaker 1:</b></v> Some people prefer modern architecture,

11
00:01:06.423 --> 00:01:10.775
but buildings from the past can be good for a city.

12
00:01:11.084 --> 00:01:20.268
Old houses and palaces are interesting because they tell us about how people once lived and worked.

13
00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:26.664
Some are also very beautiful, so visitors come to the city to see them.

14
00:01:28.801 --> 00:01:36.715
<v><b>Male Speaker 2:</b></v> The job of a police detective is very different from what we see on TV.

15
00:01:36.808 --> 00:01:42.337
In real life, detectives work on many different crimes, not only murders.

16
00:01:42.492 --> 00:01:46.487
In the UK, some detectives start as police officers

17
00:01:46.526 --> 00:01:49.918
and then do an exam when they have enough experience.

18
00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:53.658
Others train for the job when they finish university.

19
00:01:57.328 --> 00:02:02.748
<v><b>Male Speaker 3:</b></v> Most of us feel safe in our houses because we spend a lot of time there.

20
00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:08.200
But many people go to hospital each year because of something that happened at home.

21
00:02:08.386 --> 00:02:15.370
There are dangers in all of the rooms, but one big problem is people falling over furniture in the living room.